    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\nA Coder-backed Cloud session loses coding-agent conversation continuity when the workspace is auto-paused and resumed. The desktop briefly shows `Terminal disconnected - reattaching...`; after recovery, the terminal is backed by a fresh Claude process/conversation.\n\n**Source:** Live design-partner POC report on 2026-08-31\n**Reported by:** Prateek\n**Analyzed against:** `a78744b0e` (preview release `terminal-preview-7a8856f63`)\n**Priority:** high \u2014 session continuity and uncommitted workspace state can be lost on a normal idle pause\n**Confidence:** High\n\n## Reproduction\n1. Create a Cloud project/session using the Coder sandbox provider and the current Docker-based Linux template.\n2. Let the session reach the configured idle-pause threshold.\n3. Open the session terminal so the desktop requests terminal tickets and wakes the workspace.\n4. Observe `Terminal disconnected - reattaching...` while Coder resumes.\n5. After recovery, inspect the workspace process: Claude was launched afresh with `--session-id` rather than restored with `--resume`.\n\n## Live evidence\n- Session `00ac3284-fd41-4d53-9077-a0cf7cc1f01e` auto-paused at `2026-09-01T02:15:36Z`; its replacement `ao-worker` started at `02:16:57Z` and Claude at `02:17:08Z`.\n- Session `07ad6206-aeb5-4b8e-b3fb-4aa61ee69241` auto-paused at `02:16:36Z`; its replacement `ao-worker` started at `02:18:43Z` and Claude at `02:18:50Z`.\n- Worker epochs advanced to 15 and 16 and new agent terminal rows were created.\n- The Coder containers mount a durable volume only at `/home/coder`.\n- `/workspace/repository` exists only in the container filesystem.\n\n## Root Cause\n`cloud/internal/reconcile/reconciler.go:workerSpec` hardcodes:\n- `AO_WORKSPACE_DIR=/workspace/repository`\n- `AO_DATA_DIR=/workspace/.ao/worker`\n- `HOME=/workspace/.ao/home`\n- `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/workspace/.ao/home/.claude`\n- `CODEX_HOME=/workspace/.ao/home/.codex`\n\n`cloud/internal/sandbox/coder/client.go:bootstrapCommand` creates and owns `/workspace`, but the approved Coder template's persistent volume is mounted at `/home/coder`. Stopping and starting the workspace recreates the container and discards `/workspace`.\n\n`cloud/internal/workerexec/command.go:interactiveRestoreIdentity` correctly restores only when the Claude JSONL exists under `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`. Because that directory was discarded, it falls back to a fresh launch. The same path mismatch also puts the checked-out repository and uncommitted changes at risk.\n\n## Fix\nDefine a provider-specific durable workspace root contract. For Coder:\n- use a template-backed persistent directory for repository, AO worker data, harness homes, and repository credentials;\n- make the persistent path configurable or derive it from an explicit Coder template contract rather than assuming `/home/coder`;\n- validate persistence across a stop/start before enabling idle pause;\n- test Coder pause/resume for repository files and Claude/Codex conversation restoration.\n\nThe terminal UI should separately communicate `Resuming workspace` and `Restoring agent`, but that does not replace the persistence fix.\n\n## Related\n- [PR #4624](https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4624) \u2014 Coder sandbox provider integration.\n",
